#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# select_first

#% text
# `select_first(xs, f)` gives the first element `x` of `xs` with `f(x)` `true`; `select_first(xs, f, d)` gives `d` when there is none.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Without a default, no match is `failure(not_found, select_first)`.

#% item
# The values of an association are its elements.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
select_first([1, 3, 4, 6], is_even)
#% output
#= 4

#% cell
select_first([1, 3], is_even, none)
#% output
#= none

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The values of an association:

#% cell
select_first(assoc(a -> 1, b -> 2), is_even)
#% output
#= 2

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `select`, `first_case`
